      "value": "@{602d8fd1ed0cbf3933eb2a63|full_name}\n\nThe strength of a queue is that people can join it and wait without having to request again when the instance isn't full anymore. A queue keeps your instance full with minimum effort on your part and event attendees have a good idea of how long they may need to wait to get into the event.\n\nWhat this proposed instance type is actually solving for is making sure that your staff is in the world while allowing for guests to join. Finer control over who can join a group instance would better serve us. \n\nLet us reserve so many slots for specific group roles. If I could set 30 instance slots for staff members only and let group members fill the rest that would be perfect. \n\nLet us update group instance settings after opening the instance. This way an instance could only allow staff roles to join at first and then you could update the instance to allow attendee roles to join once you are ready. Imagine if we could change the instance cap instead of it being tied to map size as well.\n\nThis group instance type feels like a bandaid fix to running events in groups currently, but it is one I would welcome even if I wouldn't use it myself. We desperately need more tools for group instances. At the very least, this would eliminate the need for host accounts and I would think VRChat would prefer us only play on one account and not share a host account among staff.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
